# /lib/beacon/verbs -- the system tier of the presentation verb table
# (BEACON.md 7; docs/HALCYON.md 13.6 "obj interaction"). One rule per line:
#
#   <type> <label> <command template...>
#
# The menu on a presented object offers the labels for its type; choosing
# one runs the template with every `{}` replaced by the RESOLVED ref,
# single-quoted for ut (rc's rule: '' is the one escape) -- the command
# acts on exactly the ref the menu displayed. Types are BEACON.md 12.2's:
# path, pid, url, commit, user, layout. Baked from usr/lib/beacon/verbs.default.
#
# Quoting makes the ref ONE argument; only `--` keeps a ref that begins with
# `-` out of option position. It goes wherever the program takes it (ls,
# stat, cat); hexdump, nora, wget and the ut builtins do not yet (queued).

path   ls        ls -l -- {}
path   cat       cat -- {}
path   stat      stat -- {}
path   cd        cd {}
path   edit      nora {}
path   hexdump   hexdump {}
pid    kill      kill {}
url    fetch     wget {}
# A saved layout's ref is its NAME (HALCYON.md 13.7; `halcyon layout list`
# presents them): restore rebuilds it beside the console, save overwrites it
# with the live tree, delete removes the session-tier file. A name never
# begins with `-`, so no `--` is needed.
layout restore   halcyon layout restore {}
layout save      halcyon layout save {}
layout delete    halcyon layout delete {}
